  "method": "OpenStreetMap way 907808191, named 'ORNL Spallation Neutron Source' (amenity=research_institute), fetched via the Nominatim /lookup endpoint with polygon_geojson=1 (Overpass itself refused every connection attempt for most of this session; see the worklog's method note). Nodes kept verbatim, no simplification. This is the outer boundary of the whole SNS linac/ring/target complex, not a trace of Neutrino Alley itself: Neutrino Alley is a basement corridor inside the target building, somewhere within this ~0.7 x 1.4 km footprint, and no more specific public source or OSM element for it was found this session. Used here, honestly widened in `accuracy_m`, as the best available anchor for the detector-hosting site.",
